# QA: Fix popover containerPadding for flip detection
Date: 2026-07-25
Scope: All dropdown popovers across the app

## Change
- `popover.tsx:15` — `containerPadding` from 0 → 16 (shared ComboBox/Select popover)
- `multi-select.tsx:251` — `containerPadding` from 0 → 16 (standalone AriaPopover)

## Root cause
`containerPadding={0}` meant React Aria's auto-flip (Floating UI) only triggered at the
very viewport edge. When a ComboBox/Select was in the middle or bottom of a scrollable form,
the popover opened downward and covered sibling "+ Them" buttons.

## Affected instances fixed (8 vulnerable patterns)
All use ComboBox → shared Popover, or SearchableSelect (already had viewportPadding=16):
1. Customer picker (csc-customer-picker) — ShipmentCreateWorkspace.tsx:489
2. Shipping line picker (csc-shipping-line-picker) — ShipmentCreateWorkspace.tsx:521
3. Route picker — LCL section (csc-route-picker) — ShipmentCreateWorkspace.tsx:543
4. Route picker — FCL per-row — ShipmentCreateWorkspace.tsx:719
5. Pickup port (cang nang) — FCL per-row — ShipmentCreateWorkspace.tsx:749
6. Dropoff port (cang ha) — FCL per-row — ShipmentCreateWorkspace.tsx:768
7. Container type picker — ContainerTypeCellPicker.tsx:46
8. CUS carrier editor — CusContainerLedger.tsx:207 (SearchableSelect, already covered)

